# CR 506.4: a single combat split across two defending players at once.
# Grizzly Bears (2/2) attacks ai; Silvercoat Lion (2/2) attacks p2 -- two
# different defenders in one combat, the case DeclareCombatBlockers used to
# assume away (block.go, "who is defending" used to mean attackers[0]'s
# defender only). ai's Hill Giant (3/3) blocks the Bears; p2's Durkwood
# Boars (4/4) blocks the Lion. Each defender is asked separately and only
# about the attacker(s) actually attacking them: ai never sees the Lion, p2
# never sees the Bears, and neither blocker crosses over to the other
# attacker. Both attackers take lethal damage and die (2/2 vanillas against
# 3 and 4 power respectively); both blockers survive.
#
# human has a real library card: CR 103.8a's "the first player skips their
# first draw step" is two-player-only (drawStep, turn.go), so in this
# three-player game human draws for real during the Draw step "advance 5"
# passes through, same as ai or p2 would on their own first turn here.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1,2
queue attacktarget ai
queue attacktarget p2
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 3=1
queue blocks 4=2
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
# One more advance for the state-based-action check that moves both
# lethally damaged attackers to the graveyard.
advance
